    "explanation": "To both parties.\n\nTHE CHARGE. This was an upfront-quoted trip. EV-FARE-00517 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd of SGD 28.00, and you were charged charged_total of SGD 67.50. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time lines were fixed at booking, so no distance-or-time refund is available on the route however the trip is characterised, and POL-RD-02 does not run. What remains is POL-RD-11(a): every dollar by which charged_total exceeds quoted_fare_sgd plus the pass-through and statutory lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09 is refunded in full. The only such line here is the SGD 6.00 Changi Airport surcharge on EV-FARE-00517, and it is properly chargeable because the trip ORIGINATED at Changi Terminal 3 (pickup label on EV-TRIP-00517); erp_gantries and tolls_erp are 0.00 and waiting_time_fee is 0.00. The refund is therefore 67.50 - 28.00 - 6.00 = SGD 33.50 to the rider. That is the 'other 33' the rider could not account for.\n\nTHE ROUTE. No deviation is established. Against an optimal_distance_km of 19.6 (EV-TRIP-00517) the trace measures 19.9 km - an excess of 0.3 km and about 1.53% - below both POL-RD-01 gates (more than 0.8 km AND more than 20%), so POL-RD-01 finds no deviation. The trace EV-GPS-00517 is impaired: weight_multiplier 0.39, issue codes GPS_GAP (one 620-second gap, 22:26:30-22:36:50) and LOW_COVERAGE (coverage_pct 65.6). That gap is policy-impaired under POL-RD-07(a) (over 90 s). Taking the gap as the straight line between its bounding fixes, the reading most favourable to the driver under POL-RD-07(i), still leaves only 0.3 km of excess, so the deviation limb is decided (negatively), not left undecided. The driver's account that his app crashed and later 'completed the trip by itself' is consistent with a single mid-trip telemetry dropout, and his statement that he 'didn't choose the amount' is treated as evidence supporting that the over-quote amount was not a fare the rider agreed to.\n\nESCALATION. The driver asked in the alternative for escalation under POL-RD-10(3). It is not triggered. POL-RD-10(3), like POL-RD-07(iii), exists where a deviation would have to be established ON AN IMPAIRED TRACE without an independent corroborating source named in POL-RD-07(ii). Here no deviation is or can be established on this trace - the excess is below the POL-RD-01 gate even on the driver-favourable straight-line reading - and the money does not rest on the trace at all: it rests on EV-FARE-00517 and EV-TRIP-00517, both COMPLETE at weight 1.0, so POL-GEN-02(2) caps confidence at 1.0 and the 0.39 trace does not drag it down. Confidence is 0.85, above the 0.70 floor, so POL-RD-10(1) does not fire either.\n\nCLAIMS ANSWERED. The rider's upfront-fare claim under POL-RD-11 and her overcharge arithmetic under POL-RD-11(a)/POL-RD-09 are accepted; they carry the ruling. Her no-deviation claim (POL-RD-01/POL-RD-11) is accepted, with the impairment of EV-GPS-00517 disclosed as above. Her POL-RD-04 claim is accepted: EV-CHAT-00517 is empty (message_count 0, messages []), so no rider-requested detour is in the record and the driver's unrecovered cost is not recoverable from the rider under POL-RD-11. Her POL-RD-03 claim is accepted: EV-ADVIS-00517-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 (MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no closure justifies the route or the charge. Her rate-card reconciliation point is noted - time_fare 40.50 does not match 30.0 min x 0.28 (8.40), and distance_fare 16.40 does not match 19.9 km x 0.75 (14.925) - but under POL-RD-11 those lines were fixed at booking, and it is not a POL-RD-09(4) defect (no unmatched gantry line, and the airport surcharge is properly chargeable), so it changes no amount. Her POL-RD-08 point is accepted: deviation_claims_60d 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0, so no extra beyond-the-trace corroboration burden attaches.\n\nThe driver's claims that no deviation exists (POL-RD-01), that the trace distance governs, that the impaired stretch is read in the driver's favour (POL-RD-07(i)), that the fare is upfront-quoted (POL-RD-11), and that there is no POL-RD-09(4) billing defect, are all accepted. His claim that the rider cannot discharge the POL-RD-08 burden on the deviation is accepted so far as it goes - no deviation is proven - but it does not produce NO_ACTION, because the rider's remedy does not depend on a deviation; it rests on the upfront quote against the charged total. His request for NO_ACTION is rejected: it would leave the SGD 33.50 charged over the quote in place with no chargeable basis. His POL-RD-06 point is accepted: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250, no pattern is established, and no conduct referral arises.\n\nREFERRALS. None. No clause produces one: POL-RD-06(c) needs a material deviation and a pattern (neither exists), and no POL-RD-09(4) line exists. Open question for the platform, not a referral: why an upfront-quoted trip was settled on a metered-style breakdown summing to 67.50 against a 28.00 quote; that deserves the platform's attention but does not change the remedy."
  },
