    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this was an upfront-quoted trip, and that decides the money. EV-FARE-00517 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE with a quoted fare of SGD 28.00, so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run — no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however the trip is characterised, and the metered rate-card arithmetic is not the route to the money. The amount actually charged was SGD 67.50 (charged_total). The only pass-through properly chargeable on top of the quote is the SGD 6.00 Changi Airport surcharge, because the trip originated at Changi Terminal 3 (pickup on EV-TRIP-00517); erp_gantries is empty and the waiting-time fee is 0.00, so nothing else is added back. The excess is SGD 67.50 − SGD 28.00 − SGD 6.00 = SGD 33.50, refunded in full under POL-RD-11(a). Both advocates' figure of SGD 33.50 is accepted, and the rider's observation that the time and distance lines do not reconcile with the printed rate card is noted but raises no separate escalation: those lines have counterparts in the trip record (30.0 minutes, 19.9 km), so no unmatched charge line arises, and on an upfront trip the remedy is the excess over the quote, which is what is awarded.\n\nOn the route claim: the GPS trace EV-GPS-00517 is impaired — weight 0.39, issue codes GPS_GAP (a single 620-second gap) and LOW_COVERAGE (coverage_pct 65.6) — and I have read it with that discount in mind. Trace distance of 19.9 km against a 19.6 km optimal is an excess of 0.3 km and 1.53%, below both POL-RD-01 gates, so no deviation is established on this trip. No POL-RD-06 pattern is made out either (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 against 250 completed trips in 90 days), so no conduct referral follows.\n\nThe driver asked that the charge stand, or in the alternative that the case go to a human reviewer. Both are declined. The impairment of the trace does not move the money: the deciding fact — that SGD 67.50 was charged against a SGD 28.00 quote — is carried by the fare breakdown, a complete artifact at weight 1.0, and by the driver's own account, not by the trace, so POL-RD-07(ii) and POL-RD-10(3) do not make this case terminal; there is no deviation finding resting on the impaired stretch. The driver's account that his app crashed mid-trip and 'completed the trip by itself' and that he did not choose the amount matches the recorded 620-second telemetry gap and is accepted; it confirms the SGD 33.50 was not a fare anyone set. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00517-01 (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) exonerates nothing under POL-RD-03, as both sides accept. The rider is not put to the extra POL-RD-08 corroboration burden, her profile showing deviation_claims_60d 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0."
